  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/v1/models?type=image
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  # List Models API

  Get a list of all available models for image or video generation.

  ## Endpoint
  `GET /v1/models`

  ## Authentication
  Optional. Public endpoint (no API key required).

  ## Query Parameters
  - `type` (string, optional) - Filter by model type:
    - `image` - Only image generation models
    - `video` - Only video generation models
    - Omit to get all models
  - `status` (string, optional) - Filter by status:
    - `active` - Only active models (default)
    - `beta` - Beta/preview models
    - `deprecated` - Deprecated models
  - `provider` (string, optional) - Filter by provider:
    - `google` - Google models (Gemini, Imagen, Veo)
    - `runware` - Runware models

  ## Response

  Returns an object keyed by model ID:
  ```json
  {
    "google/gemini-2.5-flash-image": {
      "id": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-image",
      "name": "Gemini 2.5 Flash Image",
      "type": "image",
      "status": "active",
      "category": "text-to-image",
      "description": "Fast and efficient image generation...",
      "providers": [
        {
          "id": "gemini",
          "model_name": "gemini-2.5-flash-image",
          "pricing": {
            "type": "fixed",
            "value": 0.02
          }
        }
      ],
      "capabilities": {
        "supportsImage": true,
        "maxInputImages": 3,
        "aspectRatios": ["1:1", "16:9", "9:16", ...],
        "maxResolution": "1024x1024"
      },
      "tags": ["fast", "multimodal", "gemini"],
      "arenaScore": null,
      "releaseDate": "2025-01-15"
    },
    "google/veo-2": {
      "id": "google/veo-2",
      "name": "Veo 2",
      "type": "video",
      ...
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Model Object Fields

  ### Core Fields
  - `id` - Unique model identifier
  - `name` - Human-readable model name
  - `type` - Model type ("image" or "video")
  - `status` - Model status ("active", "beta", "deprecated")
  - `category` - Model category (e.g., "text-to-image", "video-generation")
  - `description` - Detailed model description

  ### Provider Configuration
  - `providers` - Array of provider configurations
    - `id` - Provider ID ("gemini", "runware", etc.)
    - `model_name` - Actual model name used by provider API
    - `pricing` - Pricing information
      - `type` - "fixed", "calculated", or "post_generation"
      - `value` - Price per generation (in USD)

  ### Capabilities
  - `supportsImage` - Accepts reference images
  - `maxInputImages` - Maximum reference images allowed
  - `minInputImages` - Minimum reference images required
  - `aspectRatios` - Supported aspect ratios
  - `maxResolution` - Maximum output resolution
  - `supportsTextToImage` - Supports text-only generation
  - `supportsImageToImage` - Supports image-to-image
  - Model-specific capabilities (e.g., `supportsGoogleSearch` for Gemini 3 Pro)

  ### Metadata
  - `tags` - Array of tags for categorization
  - `arenaScore` - LLM Arena score (if applicable)
  - `releaseDate` - Model release date
  - `examples` - Array of example use cases

  ## Examples

  ### Get All Image Models
  ```bash
  GET /v1/models?type=image
  ```

  ### Get All Video Models
  ```bash
  GET /v1/models?type=video
  ```

  ### Get Active Models Only
  ```bash
  GET /v1/models?status=active
  ```

  ### Get Google Models
  ```bash
  GET /v1/models?provider=google
  ```

  ## Use Cases

  ### Display Available Models in UI
  Use this endpoint to dynamically populate model dropdowns in your application.

  ### Check Model Capabilities
  Check what features a model supports before making a generation request:
  - Max reference images
  - Supported aspect ratios
  - Pricing information

  ### Model Discovery
  Discover new models as they're added to the platform without updating your code.

  ## Response Codes
  - `200 OK` - Successfully returned models list
  - `400 Bad Request` - Invalid query parameters
}
